103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535797 true] [17592186366701 1111 #uuid "52a542da-2362-574f-8242-1d88218157f8" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366702 1034 "∅,{1},{1,2}" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535797 true] [17592186366702 1111 #uuid "411eb26f-b7fa-5fb0-a917-3a47bf812fd5" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366703 1034 "{-1},{-1,1}" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535797 true] [17592186366703 1111 #uuid "36838164-1898-5a90-bc6f-fb0362ccc6f7" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366704 1034 "∅,{-1},{1},{-1,1}" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535797 true] [17592186366704 1111 #uuid "d543962f-3554-5233-9ff7-f5d74edc4679" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366706 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1089 "q-37261" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1100 "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={2{n}^{2}∣n\\in N,1\\le n\\le 3}$ and $B={2,0,8,18}?$ \n\n- $A⊈B$\n- $∅⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊇B$" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1113 #uuid "b134330d-030e-578e-9b6f-f2b714ed45de" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366705 1145 "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3}$ into the formula $2{n}^{2},$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {1}^{2}=2 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2}=8 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {3}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={2,8,18}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊈B$ is false. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $∅⊆B$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is false. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535797 true] [17592186366706 1000 #edb/ref 1759